WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.178
Episode 6 put the dotted card on a locked
Background layer, under everything else.

2
00:00:05.217 --> 00:00:09.837
Today I'll lighten its dots without touching
the lock or nudging what sits on top.

3
00:00:09.903 --> 00:00:13.213
And we'll see what decides
which element ends up in front.

4
00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:14.800
First, the cover.

5
00:00:14.927 --> 00:00:18.407
Nothing is locked here, and
the card lies under the title.

6
00:00:18.486 --> 00:00:20.686
Click the title, and you get the title.

7
00:00:20.766 --> 00:00:25.466
Click again on the same spot, and the
selection steps down a level, to the card.

8
00:00:25.674 --> 00:00:28.054
One more click wraps back to the title.

9
00:00:28.126 --> 00:00:31.533
That's the quickest way when
you're already on the top element.

10
00:00:31.612 --> 00:00:35.152
One catch: a click on the dot in
the middle doesn't step down.

11
00:00:35.269 --> 00:00:37.669
That's the pivot, so click beside it.

12
00:00:37.876 --> 00:00:42.494
Alt-click, or Option-click on a Mac,
digs the same way but never grabs,

13
00:00:42.494 --> 00:00:44.825
so nothing can move by accident.

14
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.930
Alt-click the subtitle:
you get the subtitle.

15
00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.090
Again, same spot: the card.

16
00:00:50.295 --> 00:00:53.596
When the pile is deep, or
things look alike, right-click,

17
00:00:53.596 --> 00:00:55.814
or two-finger click on a trackpad.

18
00:00:55.943 --> 00:00:59.375
The menu lists everything under
the pointer, top to bottom,

19
00:00:59.375 --> 00:01:01.253
with its type and its layer.

20
00:01:01.458 --> 00:01:06.477
Hover a row, and its element is outlined
on the page, so you know which is which.

21
00:01:06.565 --> 00:01:08.825
Click Rect, and the card is selected.

22
00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:10.248
Now the job.

23
00:01:10.395 --> 00:01:13.865
In Appearance, Fill, I'll take
the paler peach of the circle.

24
00:01:13.947 --> 00:01:16.897
The dots step back, and
the title hasn't moved.

25
00:01:17.103 --> 00:01:18.943
On to the recipe pages.

26
00:01:19.065 --> 00:01:23.155
Here the card sits on Background,
which we locked in episode 6.

27
00:01:23.235 --> 00:01:26.585
Right-click the title, and
only the title is listed.

28
00:01:26.802 --> 00:01:30.092
All three canvas tricks skip
locked and hidden layers.

29
00:01:30.195 --> 00:01:31.915
That's what locking is for.

30
00:01:31.959 --> 00:01:33.739
Escape closes the menu.

31
00:01:33.945 --> 00:01:35.935
The Layers panel skips nothing.

32
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.239
Under Background, click Rect,
and the card is selected,

33
00:01:39.239 --> 00:01:41.374
even though its layer is locked.

34
00:01:41.579 --> 00:01:44.729
No handles, so it can't
be dragged or resized.

35
00:01:44.779 --> 00:01:47.189
But Element Properties works as usual.

36
00:01:47.323 --> 00:01:49.373
Fill: the same paler peach.

37
00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.270
Background is still locked,
and nothing else has moved.

38
00:01:53.474 --> 00:01:56.134
While the card's selected,
look at Geometry.

39
00:01:56.248 --> 00:01:58.018
Its Z-Index is 1.

40
00:01:58.071 --> 00:02:01.441
Click the title's row:
its Z-Index is 1 as well.

41
00:02:01.648 --> 00:02:06.357
Same number, yet the title is on top,
because layer order counts first.

42
00:02:06.419 --> 00:02:10.467
Everything on Content sits in
front of everything on Background.

43
00:02:10.672 --> 00:02:13.872
Z-Index only sorts
elements within one layer.

44
00:02:14.016 --> 00:02:16.336
Watch: I'll give the card 99.

45
00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:19.235
Nothing moves; it stays under Content.

46
00:02:19.379 --> 00:02:21.159
Control Z puts it back.

47
00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:25.360
To bring something forward past a
layer, move it there with Move to,

48
00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.544
or drag its layer up by the grip.

49
00:02:27.749 --> 00:02:29.059
Let's export.

50
00:02:29.125 --> 00:02:34.955
The PDF is drawn a layer at a time, back
to front, in the same order as the canvas.

51
00:02:35.159 --> 00:02:37.139
On the cover, lighter dots.

52
00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:41.420
And on a recipe page, lighter
dots too, still under every word.

53
00:02:41.626 --> 00:02:44.166
So: click again for
what's right underneath.

54
00:02:44.227 --> 00:02:46.157
Alt-click when nothing may move.

55
00:02:46.302 --> 00:02:51.066
Right-click to see the whole pile, and use
the Layers panel for anything locked or

56
00:02:51.066 --> 00:02:51.722
hidden.

57
00:02:51.755 --> 00:02:54.515
Next time: the order a
grid does things in.
